  "_comment": "Default widget layout anchors, authored in half-cell tracks (GridLayout::TRACKS_PER_CELL = 2). Widgets not listed here are auto-placed. Two dimensions: LAYOUT VARIANT then BREAKPOINT. 'anchors' is the base (landscape) table; 'variants' holds per-layout overrides keyed exactly like the ui_xml/ override directories and resolved most-specific-first via LayoutManager::variant_chain() — a PORTRAIT panel takes variants.portrait, a TINY_PORTRAIT panel takes variants.tiny_portrait then variants.portrait, and anything unmatched falls back to 'anchors'. Breakpoint keys are named, not indexed: micro(0), tiny(1), small(2), medium(3), large(4), xlarge(5), xxlarge(6) — see include/ui_breakpoint.h. Every landscape tier is spelled out because they no longer share a track count: micro and medium are 12 cols, tiny and small are 10, large and xlarge are 16. xxlarge falls through to xlarge (same cell size, wider panel). Track counts are measured from the real content box per resolution — see tests/unit/test_grid_square_cells.cpp kMeasured.",
